{"title":"Career Roadmap: Family Counsellor","role":"Family Counsellor","summary":"A Family Counsellor supports individuals and families dealing with relationship difficulties, parenting concerns, communication problems, family transitions and other psychosocial challenges.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (General / Honours)","Course":"Human Development / Early Childhood Development"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build foundations in human development, family systems, communication, counselling skills, child development and ethical support"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Family Counsellor supports individuals and families dealing with relationship difficulties, parenting concerns, communication problems, family transitions and other psychosocial challenges."},{"type":"p","text":"Because Family Counsellor is a professional counselling role, a B.Sc. in Human Development/Early Childhood Development should be treated as a foundation, not automatically as sufficient qualification for every professional counselling position. Employers and jurisdictions may require relevant postgraduate counselling/psychology qualifications, supervised practice, professional registration or other eligibility requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest pathway combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Human Development","Psychology","Counselling Training","Family Systems","Child Development","Supervised Practice","Ethics"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Human development + psychology fundamentals"},{"text":"Developmental psychology, sociology, communication"},{"text":"Development case studies"},{"text":"Treating human behaviour superficially"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Counselling foundations"},{"text":"Communication, family dynamics, child development"},{"text":"Role-play/counselling exercises"},{"text":"No practical interpersonal skills"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Family support + assessment"},{"text":"Family systems, parenting, community work"},{"text":"Supervised fieldwork"},{"text":"Attempting clinical work without training"}],[{"text":"Year 4*"},{"text":"Professional counselling preparation"},{"text":"Counselling methods, ethics, referral systems"},{"text":"Internship + case documentation"},{"text":"No supervised experience"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"*Applicable where the B.Sc. program is four years."}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Introduction to human development"},{"text":"General psychology"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Human relationships"},{"text":"Child development fundamentals"},{"text":"Academic writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental psychology"},{"text":"Cognitive development"},{"text":"Emotional development"},{"text":"Social development"},{"text":"Family structures"},{"text":"Parenting fundamentals"},{"text":"Observation techniques"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 3"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Counselling fundamentals"},{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"Empathy"},{"text":"Rapport building"},{"text":"Communication barriers"},{"text":"Basic interviewing"},{"text":"Personality and individual differences"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 4"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Family systems"},{"text":"Parenting and family relationships"},{"text":"Adolescent development"},{"text":"Behavioural concerns"},{"text":"Family communication"},{"text":"Conflict resolution"},{"text":"Community resources"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 5"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Counselling theories"},{"text":"Case conceptualization"},{"text":"Family counselling approaches"},{"text":"Child and adolescent counselling fundamentals"},{"text":"Crisis identification"},{"text":"Referral systems"},{"text":"Professional ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 6"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Counselling practice"},{"text":"Group work"},{"text":"Family interventions"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Supervised fieldwork"},{"text":"Mental-health awareness"},{"text":"Internship preparation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 7–8, if applicable"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced counselling methods"},{"text":"Family counselling practicum"},{"text":"Child/family welfare"},{"text":"Research methods"},{"text":"Capstone"},{"text":"Supervised internship"}]}]},{"heading":"Human Development Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand development across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Infancy"},{"text":"Early childhood"},{"text":"Middle childhood"},{"text":"Adolescence"},{"text":"Emerging adulthood"},{"text":"Adulthood"},{"text":"Older adulthood"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical development"},{"text":"Cognitive development"},{"text":"Language development"},{"text":"Emotional development"},{"text":"Social development"},{"text":"Moral development"},{"text":"Identity development"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important theories include concepts from:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Piaget"},{"text":"Erikson"},{"text":"Vygotsky"},{"text":"Bowlby"},{"text":"Bronfenbrenner"},{"text":"Bandura"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is to understand development in context rather than using developmental theories as rigid labels."}]},{"heading":"Family Systems","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to view family difficulties as interactions between people and systems rather than automatically assigning blame to one individual."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Family roles"},{"text":"Boundaries"},{"text":"Communication patterns"},{"text":"Power dynamics"},{"text":"Family hierarchy"},{"text":"Alliances"},{"text":"Conflict patterns"},{"text":"Intergenerational influences"},{"text":"Family transitions"},{"text":"Parent-child relationships"},{"text":"Sibling relationships"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important family-counselling frameworks include concepts from:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Structural Family Therapy"},{"text":"Strategic Family Therapy"},{"text":"Bowen Family Systems Theory"},{"text":"Solution-Focused approaches"},{"text":"Narrative approaches"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Specific therapeutic techniques should be practiced only through appropriate professional training and supervision."}]},{"heading":"Counselling Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"h","text":"Active Listening"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Attentive listening"},{"text":"Reflection"},{"text":"Clarification"},{"text":"Summarization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Communication"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Open-ended questions"},{"text":"Neutral language"},{"text":"Appropriate silence"},{"text":"Non-judgmental responses"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rapport"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trust"},{"text":"Respect"},{"text":"Cultural sensitivity"},{"text":"Professional boundaries"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Goal Setting"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Problem","Understanding","Goals","Options","Action","Follow-up"]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not impose solutions on clients."}]},{"heading":"Family Communication","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Poor communication"},{"text":"Repeated conflict"},{"text":"Misunderstanding"},{"text":"Emotional escalation"},{"text":"Avoidance"},{"text":"Blame patterns"},{"text":"Unclear boundaries"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Teach appropriate communication principles such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"\"I\" statements"},{"text":"Clear requests"},{"text":"Reflective responses"},{"text":"De-escalation"},{"text":"Negotiation"}]}]},{"heading":"Parenting & Early Childhood","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Since the specialization is Human Development / Early Childhood Development, build strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Attachment"},{"text":"Parenting styles"},{"text":"Early learning"},{"text":"Behaviour development"},{"text":"Emotional regulation"},{"text":"Language development"},{"text":"Social development"},{"text":"School readiness"},{"text":"Parent-child interaction"},{"text":"Positive discipline"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid framing normal developmental variation as a disorder."},{"type":"p","text":"When developmental or clinical concerns arise, understand when to refer to qualified professionals such as psychologists, psychiatrists, pediatricians, speech-language professionals or other specialists."}]},{"heading":"Adolescent & Family Support","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand common family challenges involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic pressure"},{"text":"Parent-child conflict"},{"text":"Peer relationships"},{"text":"Identity development"},{"text":"Digital-media use"},{"text":"Communication difficulties"},{"text":"Family transitions"},{"text":"Independence"},{"text":"Career decisions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The counsellor should distinguish between normal developmental challenges and situations requiring specialized mental-health assessment."}]},{"heading":"Conflict Resolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conflict identification"},{"text":"De-escalation"},{"text":"Perspective-taking"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Mediation fundamentals"},{"text":"Collaborative problem-solving"},{"text":"Boundary setting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Basic Conflict Process"},{"type":"flow","items":["Listen","Identify Issues","Separate Positions from Needs","Explore Options","Agree on Actions","Follow Up"]},{"type":"p","text":"Family counselling is not about deciding who is \"right.\""}]},{"heading":"Mental-Health Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Family Counsellor should recognize situations that may require referral."},{"type":"p","text":"Develop basic awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Depression"},{"text":"Anxiety"},{"text":"Trauma"},{"text":"Substance-use concerns"},{"text":"Self-harm risk"},{"text":"Suicidal thoughts"},{"text":"Domestic violence"},{"text":"Child abuse"},{"text":"Severe behavioural concerns"},{"text":"Psychosis"},{"text":"Eating disorders"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A counsellor at this level should not diagnose or independently treat conditions outside their professional scope."},{"type":"h","text":"Immediate Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"If there is:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Imminent self-harm/suicide risk"},{"text":"Serious violence"},{"text":"Child abuse"},{"text":"Domestic violence"},{"text":"Immediate danger"}]},{"type":"p","text":"the priority is safety, emergency support and appropriate referral, not continuing an ordinary counselling session."}]},{"heading":"Assessment Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the difference between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Screening"},{"text":"Assessment"},{"text":"Diagnosis"},{"text":"Counselling"},{"text":"Psychotherapy"},{"text":"Referral"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand basic information gathering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Presenting concern"},{"text":"Family structure"},{"text":"Developmental history"},{"text":"Relationships"},{"text":"Strengths"},{"text":"Stressors"},{"text":"Support systems"},{"text":"Risk factors"},{"text":"Protective factors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Psychometric tools should only be administered/interpreted when the professional has the appropriate training and authorization."}]},{"heading":"Case Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn professional documentation:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Client intake"},{"text":"Presenting concerns"},{"text":"Background"},{"text":"Goals"},{"text":"Session notes"},{"text":"Intervention summary"},{"text":"Progress"},{"text":"Referrals"},{"text":"Follow-up"},{"text":"Closure"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Maintain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Secure records"},{"text":"Appropriate access controls"},{"text":"Professional boundaries"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not include unnecessary sensitive information in case records."}]},{"heading":"Ethics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Important principles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Informed consent"},{"text":"Respect"},{"text":"Non-discrimination"},{"text":"Professional boundaries"},{"text":"Competence"},{"text":"Appropriate referral"},{"text":"Record security"},{"text":"Conflict of interest management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important Limitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Confidentiality has legal and professional exceptions in situations such as serious safety risks, abuse or legally required disclosure. Exact requirements depend on applicable law and professional standards."}]},{"heading":"Cultural Sensitivity","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Family counselling requires sensitivity to differences in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Culture"},{"text":"Language"},{"text":"Family structure"},{"text":"Socioeconomic background"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Gender roles"},{"text":"Generational expectations"},{"text":"Parenting practices"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The counsellor should avoid imposing personal beliefs on families."}]},{"heading":"Community & Family Support Systems","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand how families may access:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Schools"},{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Mental-health professionals"},{"text":"Child-development services"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Community organizations"},{"text":"Social workers"},{"text":"Legal support"},{"text":"Child-protection services"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong counsellor knows when another professional or service is better placed to help."}]},{"heading":"Research & Data Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research methods"},{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Qualitative interviews"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Case-study methods"},{"text":"Data interpretation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"SPSS"},{"text":"R basics"},{"text":"Python basics"},{"text":"Power BI"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential applications:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Family-support program evaluation"},{"text":"Parenting-program outcomes"},{"text":"Child-development surveys"},{"text":"Community needs assessment"}]}]},{"heading":"Projects to Build","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Parent Education Program"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop an evidence-informed program covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Child development"},{"text":"Positive communication"},{"text":"Parenting"},{"text":"Emotional regulation"},{"text":"Digital-media habits"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Objectives"},{"text":"Sessions"},{"text":"Activities"},{"text":"Evaluation method"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Family Communication Case Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze anonymized/hypothetical family scenarios."},{"type":"p","text":"Identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Communication patterns"},{"text":"Family-system factors"},{"text":"Strengths"},{"text":"Stressors"},{"text":"Possible support strategies"},{"text":"Referral requirements"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid making clinical diagnoses."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Child Development Resource Platform"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a digital resource containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental milestones"},{"text":"Parent education"},{"text":"Activity ideas"},{"text":"Family resources"},{"text":"Referral information"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Ensure developmental information is evidence-informed and clearly distinguish educational guidance from medical/clinical advice."}]},{"heading":"Advanced Capstone Project","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Digital Family Support & Counselling Resource Platform"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a platform containing:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Family Resources","Developmental Education","Screening Support","Referral Directory","Progress Tracking"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Features:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parent education"},{"text":"Child-development resources"},{"text":"Family communication exercises"},{"text":"Appointment/referral management"},{"text":"Resource library"},{"text":"Anonymous educational questionnaires"},{"text":"Progress tracking"},{"text":"Professional dashboard"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Any screening or AI component should be positioned as support/triage assistance, not autonomous diagnosis or treatment."}]},{"heading":"Specialization Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialization","Additional Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Family Counselling"},{"text":"Family systems, communication"}],[{"text":"Parent Counselling"},{"text":"Parenting, child development"}],[{"text":"Child & Family Support"},{"text":"Child development, welfare"}],[{"text":"Adolescent Counselling"},{"text":"Adolescent development"}],[{"text":"School Counselling"},{"text":"Education, student support"}],[{"text":"Marriage/Relationship Counselling"},{"text":"Couples/family systems"}],[{"text":"Community Counselling"},{"text":"Community resources"}],[{"text":"Parenting Education"},{"text":"Program design, facilitation"}],[{"text":"Family Welfare"},{"text":"Social work, welfare systems"}],[{"text":"Child Development"},{"text":"Developmental assessment"}],[{"text":"Counselling Psychology"},{"text":"Advanced psychology + counselling"}],[{"text":"Family Services"},{"text":"Case management, referrals"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Child-development centres"},{"text":"Schools"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Family-support organizations"},{"text":"Community organizations"},{"text":"Counselling centres"},{"text":"Hospitals with appropriate supervision"},{"text":"Parenting programs"},{"text":"Child-welfare organizations"},{"text":"Educational institutions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Deliverables"},{"type":"p","text":"Aim to gain experience in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Client interaction under supervision"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Parent education"},{"text":"Case documentation"},{"text":"Community programs"},{"text":"Referral coordination"},{"text":"Family-support activities"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Supervised experience is particularly important for this career."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful supplementary areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic counselling skills"},{"text":"Child development"},{"text":"Parenting education"},{"text":"Family counselling"},{"text":"Psychological first aid"},{"text":"Child safeguarding"},{"text":"Conflict resolution"},{"text":"Suicide-prevention awareness"},{"text":"Trauma-informed practice"},{"text":"Mental-health first aid"},{"text":"Communication skills"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Certificates do not automatically make someone qualified to diagnose or provide psychotherapy. Professional qualification, supervised practice and applicable registration/eligibility requirements are more important."}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Careers","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Depending on qualifications and employer requirements:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Family Support Assistant"},{"text":"Family Services Associate"},{"text":"Child & Family Support Associate"},{"text":"Parent Educator"},{"text":"Child Development Associate"},{"text":"Counselling Assistant"},{"text":"Counselling Support Worker"},{"text":"Community Support Associate"},{"text":"Family Welfare Assistant"},{"text":"Student Support Associate"},{"text":"Childcare/Development Program Coordinator"},{"text":"Family Program Assistant"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A direct Family Counsellor title may require a relevant postgraduate counselling/psychology qualification and supervised experience."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a student aiming specifically toward professional counselling, consider:"},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.A./M.Sc Psychology"},{"text":"Counselling Psychology"},{"text":"Clinical Psychology*"},{"text":"Educational Psychology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Counselling"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.A./M.Sc Counselling"},{"text":"Guidance & Counselling"},{"text":"Family Counselling"},{"text":"Child & Adolescent Counselling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Human Development"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Human Development"},{"text":"Child Development"},{"text":"Human Development & Family Studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Social Work"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MSW"},{"text":"Family & Child Welfare"},{"text":"Medical & Psychiatric Social Work"}]},{"type":"p","text":"*Clinical practice has specific qualification, supervised-training and regulatory requirements; the exact current pathway should be verified with the relevant Indian regulatory/professional authorities before presenting it as a career route."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Potential postgraduate areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Family Counselling"},{"text":"Marriage & Family Therapy"},{"text":"Counselling"},{"text":"Counselling Psychology"},{"text":"Child & Family Studies"},{"text":"Human Development"},{"text":"Family Studies"},{"text":"Social Work"},{"text":"Child & Adolescent Mental Health"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Professional licensing is country-specific. A foreign degree does not automatically authorize counselling practice in another country. The destination country's registration, accreditation, supervised-hours and professional-body requirements must be checked."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"0–2 Years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Family Support Associate","Counselling Assistant","Child/Family Program Associate"]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Family support"},{"text":"Referral coordination"},{"text":"Supervised practice"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 Years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Family Counsellor","Senior Counsellor","Family Services Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"Subject to the required professional qualifications."},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Family counselling"},{"text":"Parent support"},{"text":"Case management"},{"text":"Crisis referral"},{"text":"Group facilitation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 Years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Senior Family Counsellor","Family Services Coordinator","Program Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Program management"},{"text":"Team supervision"},{"text":"Family interventions"},{"text":"Community programs"},{"text":"Training"}]},{"type":"h","text":"8+ Years"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible directions:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Family Services Manager"},{"text":"Counselling Program Director"},{"text":"Child & Family Program Director"},{"text":"Family Counselling Specialist"},{"text":"Parenting Program Consultant"},{"text":"Family Support Organization Leader"}]}]},{"heading":"Long-Term Relevance: 2030–2046","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Family-support services are likely to increasingly combine human counselling with digital tools."},{"type":"p","text":"Important developments include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tele-counselling"},{"text":"Digital family-support platforms"},{"text":"AI-assisted documentation"},{"text":"Digital parenting education"},{"text":"Early-support screening tools"},{"text":"Family resource platforms"},{"text":"Multilingual counselling resources"},{"text":"Remote supervision"},{"text":"Data-driven family-support programs"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI should be used primarily for administrative support, education, resource discovery and decision support, with qualified professionals responsible for sensitive assessment and counselling decisions."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Human Development"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Child development"},{"text":"Adolescent development"},{"text":"Adult development"},{"text":"Family development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Counselling"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"Rapport"},{"text":"Interviewing"},{"text":"Goal setting"},{"text":"Conflict resolution"},{"text":"Family systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Family Support"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parenting"},{"text":"Parent-child relationships"},{"text":"Family communication"},{"text":"Community resources"},{"text":"Referral systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Safeguarding"},{"text":"Cultural competence"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Program evaluation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"SPSS/R basics"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Tele-counselling platforms"},{"text":"Secure documentation systems"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Portfolio Target","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parent education program"},{"text":"Family communication case-study portfolio"},{"text":"Child-development resource project"},{"text":"Family-support program evaluation"},{"text":"Counselling role-play/practical record"},{"text":"Referral-resource directory"},{"text":"Child safeguarding training"},{"text":"Supervised internship"},{"text":"Professional ethics/documentation portfolio"},{"text":"Postgraduate counselling pathway identified"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Graduate Profile"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Sc. Human Development/Early Childhood Development → Human Development → Psychology → Family Systems → Counselling Fundamentals → Child & Adolescent Development → Parenting → Communication & Conflict Resolution → Ethics & Safeguarding → Supervised Fieldwork → Relevant PG Counselling/Psychology qualification → Supervised Professional Practice → Family Counsellor → Senior Family Counsellor → Family Services Specialist/Program Manager."}]}]}